# Lines tools/pi-run must see, in this order, as whole serial lines (the Pi
# 5 only: rpi5b_2gb/fan-test.system). The fan starts at full speed,
# PWM1 counts, and after 3 s the fan follows the SoC's temperature; the
# temperature, level and speed lines between them vary, and are not checked.
NOWAYOS: fan: PWM1's channel 3 drives GPIO45 at 24 kHz: full speed for 3 s to start
NOWAYOS: fan: PWM1 is counting
NOWAYOS: fan: started: following the SoC's temperature

# Output that fails the run at once if it appears anywhere (substring match).
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!fan: gave up
!no temperature
!not counting
!could not set
!refused
!panicked
